# netbird-sync gotchas

- A Hecate user's NetBird `id` is Dex's base64 protobuf: field 1 = Authentik
  `sub`, field 2 = connector id. Decode with varint lengths; accept url-safe
  and unpadded variants. A Hecate-idp user whose id doesn't decode fails the
  run — a silent skip would hide an upstream id-format change and stop
  revocations.
- Only `issued: "jwt"` NetBird groups are managed — they're created by
  sign-in sync, never by this job. `api`-issued groups on a user are always
  preserved; claim names with no group are reported, never created.
- The `groups` claim is fetched through Authentik's property-mapping test
  endpoint (`POST /propertymappings/all/{pk}/test/`), which evaluates the
  mapping exactly as sign-in does. Don't reconstruct claims from group
  membership — they can drift. The endpoint (a POST) needs global
  `authentik_core.view_propertymapping` and `authentik_core.add_propertymapping`;
  without them Authentik falls back to an object check that 500s with
  `WrongAppError`. Test blueprint edits live with `Importer.from_string` in
  `ak shell`: `ak apply_blueprint` only accepts paths under `/blueprints`.
- Alert state lives in a job-created ConfigMap (`netbird-sync-state`),
  deliberately not in Git: ArgoCD selfHeal would revert it. The Job's Role
  can only touch ConfigMaps in its own namespace.
- The Authentik service account is a separate blueprint ConfigMap
  (`authentik-blueprint-netbird-sync`) so a missing
  `NETBIRD_SYNC_AUTHENTIK_TOKEN` env can't fail the NetBird login blueprint.
- The NetBird PAT expires in 365 days (max the API allows); expiry shows up
  as the failure email, then rotate per the README. After rotating the
  Authentik token Secret, restart authentik worker+server — env loads only
  at pod start and the blueprint `!Env` fails until then.
- No package.json reaches the pod (ConfigMap mount), so keep the TS
  CJS-safe: no top-level await; Node's module detection handles the imports.
- `PUT /api/groups/{id}` replaces peers AND resources wholesale — GET the
  group immediately before each PUT and send back the fresh name/resources.
- Setup-key peers (empty `user_id`) hold jwt groups only via a TV link;
  anything else on them is stripped. A link to a user-owned peer is reported
  as a problem and left untouched.
- TV links live on the Authentik service account: `netbird_tv_owner`
  (username) + `netbird_peer_id`. Misconfig is collected as a problem and
  thrown after all updates apply — it fails the run, never blocks revocations.
